# TestJavaToKotlinFernflowerNullability: fernflower printed as Kotlin with NullabilityPass (NULL_MARKED) verdicts,
# judged by kotlinc 2.4.0 (see maddi-run-openjdk's JavaToKotlinRatchet). Lower is better for printerCrashes and
# syntaxErrors, higher for syntaxCleanFiles and compilingFiles; `types` must not move. Write a better value here in
# the commit that earns it.
#
# 2026-10-06, first record, measured with field, parameter and return verdicts only (local verdicts stubbed: ws/maddi-null
# 44f88974 was not merged yet) and before maddi a51782475 (`!!` on a nullable for-each iterable): 761 type errors,
# 275 of them null into a non-null declaration (locals, array elements, type arguments). With local verdicts the
# numbers move: tighten them in the commit after the merge.
#
# 2026-10-06, with local verdicts (ws/maddi-null 44f88974) and maddi 3c2879328/9813419e4 (`!!` on collection and
# super() arguments, verdicts from the NULLABILITY_* properties, array initializers typed by their target,
# constructor locals): 123 files compile, 497 type errors. What remains of null into non-null is mostly array
# elements (one int[][][] table with null rows carries most of them) and type arguments: the pass's next choices.
#
# 2026-10-07, the printer's `!!` decided by NullabilityPass's smart-cast facts (Report.smartCasts(), 53a96a27, M4
# first cut), with maddi's declare-then-assign and nullable-array fixes: 125 files compile, 446 type errors.
#
